{% macro bullets(items) %}
{% for b in items %}
- {{ "**[" ~ b.label ~ "]** " if b.label }}{{ b.text }}{% for c in b.refs %} [c{{ c.id }}](#claim-{{ c.id }}){{ " (partial)" if c.entailment == "partial" }}{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}
{% set req = r.request %}
# Opportunity report — {{ req.country }} {{ req.industry }}

Run #{{ r.run_id }} · {{ req.target_customer }} · {{ req.business_model }} · pack {{ r.method.pack }}{{ " (run created with " ~ r.method.run_pack ~ ")" if r.method.run_pack != r.method.pack }} · generated {{ r.generated_at }}

> Every factual bullet cites the claims it rests on (links to **Sources** at the end). Bullets
> marked **Hypothesis** or **Assumption** are not established facts; **Recommendation** bullets
> are proposals. Quotes are shown in the original language with an English translation. Only
> short excerpts are exported, never full page text.

